  "notes": "Piano-and-voice soul in the Kanye / GOOD Music orbit, 2004–2010. The research gives \"79–100 straight\" and marks the band edges `[LOW-CONF]`, so the band is used as written with the mode at 88 and `halfTime` false. The drum grammar has an unusual starting point: \"the signature record has **no drums at all** — grand piano, strings and harmonica only\", with a chopped-soul-sample kit elsewhere, itself marked `[LOW-CONF]`. Both halves are encoded honestly: a 0.3 `beatSkipProb` and a one-to-three-hit kick are how a model says \"the drums may not be there\", the hat lane sits at an 8th base and 0.12 fill density, and the snare is pushed 3–8 ms with `quantizeStrength` at 0.64 for the sampled, unquantised feel. Harmony is the identifying parameter: \"60s/70s soul harmony — I–vi–ii–V families with 7ths and 9ths, 4- and 8-bar cycles, gospel voice-leading\", and the sourced key is F major, with the main progression derived from a transposed Stevie Wonder cycle — so every family is diatonic-major functional, unusual in this minor-leaning lane. \"Tenor lead with restrained melisma and conversational phrasing\" is the 0.78 step share and the 3–8 density; \"countermelody from strings or harmonica\" is the counter at +12 with `answer_lick` leading. The bass is \"piano left hand as the bass on the ballads; on the produced cuts a sampled bass under a filtered soul loop\" — a real bass part with walking cells and no `bass808` block. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every velocity and density number and `swing.amount` 0.58. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `F`, and the remaining values `Bb`, `C`, `Eb`, `Dm`, together with all 5 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
